0..77 Comment "//! An update through an exclusive view of a held pair, answering as the copy"
78..96 Comment "//! it stands for."
97..100 Comment "//!"
101..177 Comment "//! The view lends the held value, the body builds the new one, and `resume`"
178..257 Comment "//! writes it back. The exclusivity conjecture says a runtime may build the new"
258..336 Comment "//! value in the held value\'s own block when nothing else holds it. No program"
337..414 Comment "//! can tell the difference, and these answers are what such a rebuild keeps."
415..418 Comment "//!"
419..495 Comment "//! Each item runs on both tiers. Normalisation by evaluation runs no memory"
496..570 Comment "//! form, so the stated answers are the reference. A copy taken before the"
571..640 Comment "//! update keeps its value, the independence the conjecture rests on."
641..644 Comment "//!"
645..708 Comment "//! - owes: #3205 — the rebuild in the held value\'s own block"
709..789 Comment "//! - see: `crates/runtime-emitter/src/run.rs` — where the rebuild lands today"
790..859 Comment "//! - cites: [Racordon-2020-formal_definition_swifts_value_semantics]"
860..863 Comment "//!"
864..1030 Comment "//! [Racordon-2020-formal_definition_swifts_value_semantics]: https://archive-ouverte.unige.ch/unige:145490 \"Racordon, A Formal Definition of Swift\'s Value Semantics\""
